WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.212
Is 5G just faster internet on your

2
00:00:02.212 --> 00:00:02.944
phone?

3
00:00:02.944 --> 00:00:04.906
Speed is only one of three things

4
00:00:04.906 --> 00:00:06.634
it was designed to change.

5
00:00:07.034 --> 00:00:08.567
The global telecom body,

6
00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:10.947
the ITU, named three uses:

7
00:00:10.947 --> 00:00:13.152
much faster mobile broadband,

8
00:00:13.152 --> 00:00:15.950
ultra-reliable links with almost no delay,

9
00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:18.387
and huge numbers of connected machines.

10
00:00:18.786 --> 00:00:21.131
Its targets include peak downloads of twenty

11
00:00:21.131 --> 00:00:22.745
gigabits a second,

12
00:00:22.745 --> 00:00:25.415
and delays of just one millisecond for

13
00:00:25.415 --> 00:00:28.504
critical links, fast enough for remote control

14
00:00:28.504 --> 00:00:29.721
of machines.

15
00:00:30.121 --> 00:00:31.619
And it aims to connect a million

16
00:00:31.619 --> 00:00:34.090
devices in a single square kilometre.

17
00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:37.160
That density is what lets factories,

18
00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:40.295
farms and cities link sensors and machines,

19
00:00:40.295 --> 00:00:42.141
not just people.

20
00:00:42.141 --> 00:00:44.171
This is the Internet of Things.

21
00:00:44.571 --> 00:00:46.382
India built a 5G test bed with

22
00:00:46.382 --> 00:00:48.693
the IITs from twenty eighteen,

23
00:00:48.693 --> 00:00:51.189
auctioned spectrum in twenty twenty-two,

24
00:00:51.189 --> 00:00:52.895
and launched services on the first of

25
00:00:52.895 --> 00:00:54.298
October that year.

26
00:00:54.698 --> 00:00:55.499
For GS Three,

27
00:00:55.499 --> 00:00:56.997
link 5G to three words:

28
00:00:56.997 --> 00:01:00.014
spectrum, latency, and the Internet of Things.

